  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your stones together! A line of 3 stones is impossible to capture from the front. If you leave a lone stone in the middle of the board, your opponent will easily slide two pieces around it to 'Pincer' it into oblivion.\n\nThe 'Sacrificial Bait': Move a stone into a position where it can be captured. When the opponent moves their piece to complete the capture, use your next turn to capture BOTH the opponent's pieces that were closing in. This 'Counter-Pincer' is the core of Petteia combat.\n\nPositional Strangle: Don't focus only on capturing pieces. Focus on 'Territory Control'. If you can block your opponent's access to the center of the board, their pieces will be stuck on the edges where they have fewer liberties. Use your stones to create 'Walls' that force the opponent into a corner where they can be captured more effectively.",
    Player: "Keep your stones together! A line of 3 stones is impossible to capture from the front. If you leave a lone stone in the middle of the board, your opponent will easily slide two pieces around it to 'Pincer' it into oblivion.\n\nThe 'Sacrificial Bait': Move a stone into a position where it can be captured. When the opponent moves their piece to complete the capture, use your next turn to capture BOTH the opponent's pieces that were closing in. This 'Counter-Pincer' is the core of Petteia combat.\n\nPositional Strangle: Don't focus only on capturing pieces. Focus on 'Territory Control'. If you can block your opponent's access to the center of the board, their pieces will be stuck on the edges where they have fewer liberties. Use your stones to create 'Walls' that force the opponent into a corner where they can be captured more effectively.",
